<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cursus publicus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The cursus publicus was the state courier and transport service of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, established by Augustus, with relay stations along the main roads. It carried official messages, officials and goods. The system continued in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, supporting imperial communication and administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cursus-publicus.jpg" alt="Cursus publicus" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abraham Ortelius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tabula_Itineraria_Ex_Illustri_Peutingerorum_Biblitheca_Quae_Augustae_Vindel._Est_Beneficio_Marci_Velseri_Septemviri_Augustani_In_Lucem_Edita.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
